<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Act of Security 1704</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1704">1704</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Act of Security</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Act of Security 1704 was a law of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-of-scotland">Parliament of Scotland</a> that reserved its right to choose a different successor to Queen Anne from the one chosen by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, unless <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> received guarantees of its religion, freedom and trade. It also allowed the arming of the Scottish militia. England answered with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alien-act-1705">Alien Act</a> of 1705, and the dispute led to the Union of 1707.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/act-of-security-1704.jpg" alt="Act of Security 1704" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_Scotland_(1660-1689).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
